WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:03.960
Your app is live. Your customers are real.

00:04.230 --> 00:05.860
Here’s how it grows from here.

00:06.580 --> 00:08.440
One board holds your evidence.

00:08.480 --> 00:10.580
names the one thing in the way,

00:10.580 --> 00:12.990
and proposes your next customer move.

00:12.980 --> 00:14.090
You decide.

00:14.280 --> 00:17.710
It becomes a promise, with an owner and a time.

00:17.830 --> 00:19.880
Kept promises carry their result.

00:20.030 --> 00:22.990
A missed promise stays in view until it’s recovered.

00:23.080 --> 00:24.750
Nothing waits on memory.

00:24.780 --> 00:27.550
Gates open on evidence. Never on a date.

00:27.680 --> 00:31.100
That’s what moves the count: one kept move at a time.

00:31.230 --> 00:34.540
An AI operator prepares every move. You sign it.

00:34.980 --> 00:39.440
We run our own launch on this board. From zero. In public.

00:39.830 --> 00:41.680
Yours starts with a first read.

00:42.280 --> 00:43.460
Ask for one.
